nd coastal residents can anticipate glowing nights in advance[14]. [15]If the tool succeeds, it would mark one of the first times traditional local knowledge and satellite data have been combined this directly in marine science[15].',
    questionText: '[underlined: This phenomenon, known as bioluminescence, are caused by microscopic organisms called dinoflagellates]',
    options: [
      'This phenomenon, known as bioluminescence, being caused by microscopic organisms called dinoflagellates',
      'NO CHANGE',
      'This phenomenon, known as bioluminescence, have been caused by microscopic organisms called dinoflagellates',
      'This phenomenon, known as bioluminescence, is caused by microscopic organisms called dinoflagellates',
    ],
    correctAnswer: 'D',
    explanation: 'The singular subject "phenomenon" requires the singular verb "is," not the plural "are." NO CHANGE incorrectly matches a singular subject with a plural verb. "Being caused" removes the finite verb needed to complete the sentence, creating a fragment. "Have been caused" repeats the same number disagreement, since "have" is a plural auxiliary verb. ACT Tip: A parenthetical phrase set off by commas, like "known as bioluminescence" here, never changes the number of the subject it interrupts.',
