    ],
    correctAnswer: 'D',
    explanation: 'The singular subject "garden" requires the singular verb "has," not the plural "have." NO CHANGE fails this basic agreement check. "Having grown" removes the finite verb and turns the clause into a fragment. "Had grew" pairs the past perfect auxiliary "had" with the wrong verb form; the correct past participle would be "grown," not "grew." ACT Tip: Identify the true grammatical subject first, ignoring any prepositional phrases, before checking whether the verb agrees with it.',
