l-town horological preservation in the Midwest[12]. [13]Tourists visiting Millbrook often stop to watch the hands sweep past the hour, unaware of the eleven months of labor behind the mechanism[13]. [14]For Ostrowski, the tower represents something larger than a machine, it represents a promise kept to a town\'s past[14]. [15]The restoration, in short, gave Millbrook back a piece of its identity[15].',
