    correctAnswer: 'A',
    explanation: 'NO CHANGE is correct because a comma followed by the coordinating conjunction "and" properly joins two independent clauses. Removing the comma before "so" creates a run-on sentence, since "so" here still joins two independent clauses that need punctuation before it. Adding a semicolon before "and" is nonstandard; a semicolon should either replace the comma-and-conjunction pairing entirely or not be used at all. The last option adds unnecessary commas around "noticeably," awkwardly breaking up the adverb from the verb it modifies. ACT Tip: When two independent clauses are joined by a coordinating conjunction like "and," "but," or "so," a comma belongs directly before the conjunction.',
